Z||000002||Old Lar||09-24-2000||09:39 PM||||It sounds like you should obtain the wiring diagrams so you know what you are doing.  I wouldn't start cutting any wires until you know which colored wire does what, so you can match them up between the engine harness and the car harness.  This will be most time consuming.<P>Did you get the transmission from the doner car?<P>You may need some minor modifications trying to mate the 3800 to the Fiero transmission, unless you are using a manual transmission, then you'll need more modifications.<P>May need some axle modifications and stuff like that.<P>If you run across problems, you'll soon understand why the pros charge several thousand dollars for the engine swap.||||reg||1
